    <statement><p>Find the derivative of the function <m>q(r)</m>, below.  It may be to your
advantage to simplify  first.</p>
<p><me>\displaystyle q(r)={6 r\over 6 r + 9}</me></p>
<p><m>q'(r) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{6\mathopen{}\left(6r+9\right)-6\cdot 6r}{\left(6r+9\right)^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p><me>q'(r) = \frac{6 (6 r + 9) - 36 r}{(6 r + 9)^2} 
         = \frac{54}{(6 r + 9)^2}.</me></p>
</solution>
